      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When the loss feels this absolute, the idea of \"walking away\" isn't about a physical location; it's about letting go of the *need* to keep fighting for what's already gone. You're not a ghost; you're someone who has reached the end of a very painful chapter. If the investment is zero, then the most logical move is to stop pouring effort into a void. It's a permission slip to stop performing for an audience that no longer exists.",
